# pfm installer end-to-end test

Run the serial harness with:

    go test -tags e2e -p 1 ./e2e/...

From a development machine, use `scripts/e2e-linux.sh` to run the same test
inside a Debian-based Linux container. The harness runs only with the explicit
`PFM_DEV_FENCE=1` signal, stages its source repository, and creates every HOME
and state directory under `t.TempDir()`.

The update phase needs a reachable local release tag. Set `PFM_E2E_PREVIOUS_TAG`
to the tag to use when the local clone has more than one release tag.
